{"dossier":"D17","entry_points":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_recursion_level.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_xmit_recursion.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_xmit_recursion_inc.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_xmit_recursion_dec.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_recursion_level.alt_2","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_xmit_recursion.alt_2","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_xmit_recursion_inc.alt_2","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_xmit_recursion_dec.alt_2","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netdev_start_xmit","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_start_xmit"],"text":"Nesting tracked per-CPU or per-task with read, test, inc and dec. Transmit publishes more then calls driver; wrapper refreshes time only on success."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_schedule_all","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_start_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_start_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_start_all_queues","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_wake_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_wake_all_queues","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_stop_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_stop_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_start_subqueue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_stop_subqueue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_wake_subqueue"],"text":"Start clears driver-off, stop stamps time then sets it, wake clears via wake path; forms cover queue zero, all queues or one subqueue with schedule-all via soft-irq."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_queue_set_dql_min_limit","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_queue_dql_avail","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_txq_bql_enqueue_prefetchw","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_txq_bql_complete_prefetchw","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_sent_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netdev_tx_sent_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_sent_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netdev_sent_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_completed_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_completed_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_reset_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_reset_subqueue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_reset_queue"],"text":"BQL updates minimum, queries room, prefetches paths, charges sent with stack-off, credits completions with reschedule, and resets. Wrappers use queue zero or indexed subqueue."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::__is_skb_forwardable","include/linux/netdevice.h::DEV_CORE_STATS_INC.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::DEV_CORE_STATS_INC.alt_2","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_orphan_frags","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_zcopy","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_uarg"],"text":"Forwarding needs egress up and length fit unless offload. Helper orphans zero-copy, drops on failure, else scrubs identity and clears priority."},{"sids":["include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook.alt_2","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_entry_hookfn","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_state","include/linux/nfs.h::nfs_fhandle_hash","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_dump_start"],"text":"Filter selects per-namespace tables by family under RCU and iterates or accepts; unknown warns. Hash is inverted CRC over leading bytes. Dump defaults owner then delegates; taps chain device/module."}],"exports":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::__NETIF_MSG_BIT","include/linux/netdevice.h::NETIF_MSG_DRV","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_msg_drv","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_msg_wol","include/linux/netdevice.h::is_socket_ioctl_cmd","include/uapi/asm-generic/ioctl.h::_IOC_TYPE","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_DROP_GETERR"],"text":"Log mask gives one bit per category with predicates for driver, probe, link, timer, up/down, errors, queue, irq, completion, status, data, hw, wol. Ioctl extracts type vs socket type. Verdict shifts off qualifiers and negates."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_set_xps_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netif_set_xps_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::ethtool_notify","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_rx_csum_fault"],"text":"XPS, ethtool notify and csum fault are inert and report success."},{"sids":["include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_DROP_REASON","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_nat_decode_session.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_nat_decode_session.alt_2","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_ct_attach","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_ct_get_tuple_skb","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_ct_hook","include/linux/netfilter/nf_conntrack_common.h::nf_conntrack_put"],"text":"Drop frees packet and returns error-plus-stolen with 16-bit error. Addr tests equality and masked conjunction. NAT needs hook else noop. Attach inert, tuple fails; put destroys on zero, ignores null."},{"sids":["include/linux/netlink.h::nlmsg_hdr","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_kernel_create","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_skb_clone","include/linux/netlink.h::NL_SET_ERR_MSG","include/linux/netlink.h::NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT","include/linux/netlink.h::NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT_MOD","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_filter_fn"],"text":"Header reads packet data; create uses current module; clone preserves destructor for vmalloc; ack records diagnostics tolerating absent and warning on truncate; filter is socket predicate."}],"extracts":["25c80d6ba235776ff7ac2ebd6fd65eb182bc9e6b3b398581b74438ba2db14a38","372e345acdaa68b73a670582b8f97827fead1ad990f04a8d05308ba956cdd4b5","5565a8a929ceef5d6df5529a67dd08cbce1ff37b19374117ba5d4d419498d8b1","c9ece5da5a837fd64634382a185d4eb072865028ff24f6d4932fa0005d34a28e"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_sent_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_completed_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_stop_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_cap_txqueue","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_orphan_frags","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_zcopy","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_uarg","include/linux/netdevice.h::DEV_CORE_STATS_INC.alt_2","include/linux/nfs.h::NFS_MAXFHSIZE","include/linux/nfs.h::nfs_compare_fh","include/linux/nfs.h::nfs_fhandle_hash","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK_LIST.alt_1","include/linux/netlink.h::NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT","include/linux/netlink.h::NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT_MOD","include/linux/netfilter/nf_conntrack_common.h::nf_conntrack_put"],"text":"Time ordered before off; recheck and barriers avoid wedges. Bad index warns and folds. Zero-copy copies or drops. Handles need bounds. OOR/truncate warn; release destroys on last."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_owned.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_owned.alt_2","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_xmit_set_more.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_xmit_set_more.alt_2"],"text":"Ownership and more-hint each have two builds; consumers must know active config."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_queue_set_dql_min_limit","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_queue_dql_avail","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_txq_bql_enqueue_prefetchw","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_txq_bql_complete_prefetchw","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_sent_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_completed_queue","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tx_reset_queue"],"text":"Without BQL the helpers noop and room reports zero."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::__dev_put","include/linux/netdevice.h::__dev_hold","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netdev_tracker_alloc","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tracker_alloc","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_tracker_free","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_hold","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_put","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_hold","include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_put","include/linux/netdevice.h::DEFINE_FREE","include/linux/ref_tracker.h::ref_tracker_alloc","include/linux/ref_tracker.h::ref_tracker_free"],"text":"Refs ignore null, else adjust per-CPU or shared counts with tracker coupling and replace moves bookkeeping. Tracker alone is inert."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::__NETIF_MSG_BIT","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_msg_init","include/linux/netdevice.h::can_checksum_protocol","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_intersect_features","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_get_wanted_features","include/linux/netdevice.h::net_gso_ok","include/linux/netdevice.h::skb_gso_ok","include/linux/skbuff.h::skb_has_frag_list","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_needs_gso","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_get_gro_max_size","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_get_gso_max_size"],"text":"Level maps to mask; checksum needs features; features intersect with csum expansion and wanted merge; GSO needs bits and frag-list; sizes pick v6/v4."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_xmit_set_more.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_xmit_more.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_xmit_set_more.alt_2","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_xmit_more.alt_2","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_ops_type","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_entries_get_hook_ops","include/linux/netfilter/nf_conntrack_common.h::ip_conntrack_stat","include/linux/netlink.h::NLMSG_DEFAULT_SIZE","include/linux/nfs.h::nfs_compare_fh","include/linux/nfs4.h::NFS4ERR_RESET_TO_MDS","include/linux/nfs4.h::FATTR4_WORD0_SUPPORTED_ATTRS","include/linux/nfs4.h::FATTR4_WORD2_SUPPATTR_EXCLCREAT","include/linux/nfs4.h::FATTR4_WORD0_ACL"],"text":"More has per-CPU and per-task builds. Hooks sort by priority with bounded array, trailing descriptors, tagged bits and fixed ctx. Handles compare length/bytes; seq rejects stale cid/stateid, bad stateid/seqid/xdr, resource, nofh, moved; attr mask uses three words."}],"locks":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::__netif_tx_lock","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netif_tx_lock_bh","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netif_tx_trylock","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netif_tx_unlock","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_owned.alt_1","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_lock_bh","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_unlock_bh","include/linux/netdevice.h::HARD_TX_LOCK","include/linux/netdevice.h::HARD_TX_TRYLOCK","include/linux/netdevice.h::HARD_TX_UNLOCK","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_disable"],"text":"Queue locks record CPU on acquire and clear before release with ownership test. Hard locking uses locks unless lockless (annotations only). Disable stops all queues under global BH serialization."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_addr_lock","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_addr_lock_bh","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_addr_unlock","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_addr_unlock_bh"],"text":"Address lists use dedicated lock with plain and BH forms plus nesting level."},{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::dev_nit_active","include/linux/netdevice.h::softnet_data","include/linux/netdevice.h::page_pool_bh","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK_LIST.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_nat_decode_session.alt_1"],"text":"Tap and hook lookup run under RCU; process and pool use BH locks. RPS groups cachelines; NAT dereferences hook only under RCU."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F2"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F4"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p10","crown":"A","phase":"F5"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p13","crown":"A","phase":"F6"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_tx_queue_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_queue_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_xmit_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_xmit_frozen_or_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_xmit_frozen_or_drv_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::__netif_subqueue_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_subqueue_stopped","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_dormant_on","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_dormant_off","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_testing_on","include/linux/netdevice.h::netif_testing_off","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_name","include/linux/netdevice.h::netdev_reg_state.alt_2"],"text":"Queues use driver, stack and frozen marks with single and combined predicates. Dormant/testing change on edge with linkwatch. Registration has uninit, registered, unregistering, unregistered, released, dummy with suffixes; unknown warns once; empty names use placeholder."},{"sids":["include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK_COND.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK_LIST.alt_1","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK_COND.alt_2","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK.alt_2","include/linux/netfilter.h::NF_HOOK_LIST.alt_2"],"text":"Accept continues to completion; others propagate. Conditional skips when false; list feeds queue without verdict; disabled completes directly or noops."},{"sids":["include/linux/nfs4.h::nfs4_acl_whotype","include/linux/nfs4.h::FIRST_NFS4_OP"],"text":"Ops run access 3 to remove-xattr 75 with illegal 10044; base, 4.1, 4.2 end at release-lockowner, reclaim-complete, remove-xattr."}],"structs":[{"sids":["include/linux/netdevice.h::softnet_data","include/linux/netdevice.h::page_pool_bh","include/linux/netdevice_xmit.h::netdev_xmit","include/linux/netdevice_xmit.h::MIRRED_NEST_LIMIT","include/linux/netdevice.h::XMIT_RECURSION_LIMIT","include/linux/netdevice.h::NETDEV_RSS_KEY_LEN","include/linux/netdevice.h::PTYPE_HASH_SIZE","include/linux/netdevice.h::PTYPE_HASH_MASK","include/linux/netdevice.h::anon_3"],"text":"Softnet holds polling, work, completion, output, nesting, flags, counters, RPS, backlog, IPI with optional members. Pool pairs pool/BH. Xmit holds counter/more. Limits: xmit 8, RSS 256, ptype 16/15, mirred 4; msg ordered bits plus sentinel."},{"sids":["include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_state","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_entry_hookfn","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_ops_type","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_hook_entries_get_hook_ops","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_nat_hook","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_ct_hook","include/linux/netfilter.h::nfnl_ct_hook","include/linux/netfilter.h::nf_defrag_hook","include/linux/netfilter/nf_conntrack_common.h::ip_conntrack_stat","include/linux/netfilter/nf_conntrack_zones_common.h::NF_CT_DEFAULT_ZONE_ID","include/linux/netfilter_defs.h::NF_ARP_NUMHOOKS"],"text":"Hook records link callbacks with devices, namespaces and priorities; tables hold count plus entries. Extensions expose sockopt, NAT, tracking, defrag. Stats and zones track outcomes. Tags five; info mask seven; zone zero; ARP three."},{"sids":["include/linux/netlink.h::nlmsg_hdr","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_kernel_cfg","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_ext_ack","include/linux/netlink.h::NLMSG_DEFAULT_SIZE","include/linux/netlink.h::netlink_dump_control","include/linux/netlink.h::NL_CFG_F_NONROOT_RECV","include/linux/netlink.h::NETLINK_MAX_COOKIE_LEN","include/linux/netlink.h::NLMSG_GOODSIZE.alt_1","include/linux/netlink.h::NLMSG_GOODSIZE.alt_2"],"text":"Netlink records carry addressing, config handlers, ext-ack diagnostics, dump state with fixed ctx and dump-control stages. Config uses low bits; cookie 8, message 80, ctx 48; default is goodsize minus header."},{"sids":["include/linux/nfs.h::NFS_MAXFHSIZE","include/linux/nfs4.h::nfs4_acl_whotype"],"text":"Handles use length plus 128-byte store. ACLs carry type, flags, mask and who with count prefix. Labels carry ids, length and bytes with 2048 cap. Stateids share opaque/sequence views with nine-way classifier; verifiers are opaque."},{"sids":["include/linux/nfs.h::nfs_compare_fh","include/linux/nfs4.h::FIRST_NFS4_OP","include/linux/nfs4.h::NFS4ERR_RESET_TO_MDS","include/linux/nfs4.h::nfs_ftype4"],"text":"Stable 0/1/2/-1; op bounds alias access through remove-xattr; reset 12001-12003; ftype 0-9; open claim 0-6, types 0-1, modes 0-3, limits 1-2; deleg 0-5, reasons 0-8, lock 0-4."}],"stubs":[]}
